#                     "vmexsanconnect -cluster-ready" and requires the line
#                     "[OK] Ready for vmex cluster" (FAIL otherwise; shown with
#                     the reasons). -setupstorage checks it on every node before
#                     wiping anything (-force overrides). Shared SAN storage is
#                     mandatory for VM HA; -nosan skips SAN checks for early
#                     setup. New -validate section "Network (survives reboot)":
#                     the cluster and the management (default route) interfaces
#                     must have a saved NetworkManager profile that starts at
#                     boot and holds the live address - temporary (/run),
#                     autoconnect=no, bound to another interface, or unsaved
#                     addresses are FAILs; a cabled interface without any
#                     address is a WARN.
#  1.17.0 2026-11-16  Slow BMCs (IBM IMM2): -addfence times the IPMI login; if
#                     it is slow (>8 s) or times out, it tries cipher suite 3
#                     and uses it when that works better (new option -cipher N
#                     to set it). Fence devices are created with timeouts for
#                     slow BMCs (start/monitor 60 s, reboot 180 s) and
#                     failure-timeout=120s, so one slow answer no longer stops
#                     the device for good. -bmcstatus shows WHY a fence device
#                     is not running and reports stale pending fence actions.
#  1.16.0 2026-11-16  BMC (IMM) checks. New command -bmcstatus, and a BMC section
#                     in -validate: BMC has an IP (not 0.0.0.0), is reachable
#                     from the OTHER nodes (IMM port connected, link, VLAN),
#                     fence device exists, is started, logs in from the other
#                     nodes, and points to this node's own BMC.
#  1.15.0 2026-11-15  -addfence tests the BMC from every OTHER node - the ones
#                     that will run the fence device - instead of from the
#                     node itself (a server often cannot reach its own BMC).
#                     Per node it reports network (ping) and IPMI login, and
#                     the likely cause of a failure.
#  1.14.0 2026-11-15  -addfence reads the node's own BMC address (ipmitool on
#                     that node, channels 1/2/8) and refuses an -ipaddr that
#                     belongs to another server - a swapped BMC address would
#                     power off the wrong node. A failed BMC test now explains
#                     the usual causes (no link, IPMI over LAN off, password).
#  1.13.0 2026-11-15  -setupstorage checks the LUN first: partitions, file
#                     systems or other signatures (e.g. an old Windows/GPT
#                     layout) are listed and the command stops unless -wipe is
#                     given; a partition mounted on any node always stops it.
#                     With -wipe the partition maps are removed on every node
#                     (kpartx/partx on the multipath device and its paths),
#                     the signatures erased (wipefs) and the result verified
#                     on every node before LVM is created. New option -wipe.
#  1.12.0 2026-11-15  -changeip changes the IP on the servers too (nmcli):
#                     nodes still on their old IP are reached over another
#                     address found automatically (management network);
#                     cluster stopped, all old addresses removed, then the new
#                     ones applied (swaps safe, no duplicate-address failures),
