                                     migration). Asks each root password once.
                                     Nodes may be given as IP addresses.

CLUSTER LIFECYCLE
  -create   NAME -nodes IP1 IP2 ...  Create a cluster. With IP addresses the nodes
            [-prefix node]           are named node1, node2 ... in the order given,
                                     hostnames are set, /etc/hosts is updated on
                                     every node and corosync uses these IPs.
                                     (Host names instead of IPs: no renaming.)
  -destroy  -cluster NAME            Destroy the cluster on all nodes
  -start    [node ...]               Start cluster services (default: all)
  -stop     [node ...]               Stop cluster services (default: all)
  -enable   [node ...]               Start cluster at boot (default: all)
  -disable  [node ...]               Don't start cluster at boot
  -status                            Cluster status (-full for more detail)
  -quorum                            Quorum status and configuration
  -property [key=value ...]          Show or set cluster properties

NODE MANAGEMENT
